# The virt-arm64 board's packages: its kernel and the rendered layout files for
# the QEMU/aarch64 UEFI target.
#
# Two entries and not one, because they are two decisions. mos-board-virt-arm64
# is the layout -- /etc/fstab, the ESP mount unit, the RAUC grub configuration
# -- and moves when boards/virt-arm64/board.env does. mos-kernel-virt-arm64 is
# the kernel this repository builds from boards/virt-arm64/bsp, and moves when
# its pin or its config does. The split is x64's, and for x64's reason: a
# kernel bump and a layout change are different reviews.
#
# NAMED HERE ALTHOUGH mos-board-virt-arm64 ALREADY DEPENDS ON IT. A package
# reachable only through another package's Depends is one no resolution names,
# so it never appears in _out/<board>/rootfs-packages.txt and
# tests/rootfs-manifest-test.sh reports it unreachable -- which is the right
# answer for a package nothing selects and the wrong one for the kernel.
mos-board-virt-arm64
mos-kernel-virt-arm64
